        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>chore(Data/Real): encapsulate real numbers <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38702\">#38702</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>is another experiment with the module system. I'm quite happy with how it turned out.</p>\n<p>This PR:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>hides the definition of the real numbers</li>\n<li>preserves defeqs when casting <code>Nat</code>, <code>Int</code>, <code>Rat</code>, into the reals</li>\n<li>preserves the defeq <code>x - y = x + (-y)</code> for <code>x y : Real</code></li>\n<li>removes a bunch of technical debt</li>\n<li>adjusts imports in the library, where files relied on getting access to Cauchy sequences transitively via importing the reals.</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 591744230,
        "sender_full_name": "Johan Commelin",
        "timestamp": 1777456904
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>On this PR, I get a linter error about a lemma on the p-adic numbers. Here's a test file that one could add to the PR branch.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Prime</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ_</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">])</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">diagnostics</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℚ_</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- works as expected</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- remove `module` and `public` at the top of this file to get a timeout</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I can reproduce the linter error in the test file if I remove the <code>module \\n \\n public</code> from the start of the file.</p>",
